WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.660
JWST data shows Chiriclo's inner ring grew over 50% denser while its outer ring thinned by 60%. This is Fascinating Frontiers, Episode 206, looking back over the past week, a few major threads stood out across the coverage. Venus possibly consuming its own moon remained a leading story with new modeling offered on its lack of satellites. The first direct radio signals from an exoplanet also drew repeated attention,

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:31.520
as astronomers refined detection methods.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:35.920
Chinese space plane maneuvers and expanding Artemis Accord's

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.900
signatories rounded out the recurring themes with fresh details each day.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:45.960
Researchers used stellar occultation observations from 2017 and 2022

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.380
to track changes in the rings of the Centaur Chiriclo.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:54.960
The inner ring C1R increased in opaqueness by more than 50%,

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:59.520
while the outer rings C2R decreased by about 60%.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:03.420
Chiriclo itself measures 125 kilometers in radius,

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:08.980
with the rings orbiting at 265 and 280 kilometers from its surface.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:14.460
The team of more than two dozen researchers published the findings in science advances.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:20.100
They interpret the shifts as material being gained by one ring and lost by the other.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:26.400
The observations also showed the inner ring denser overall than the outer ring in the later data said.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:34.900
Now shifting to a different story, a stacked image of 223 300 second exposures from Portugal in 2019

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:42.100
shows the Andromeda Galaxy before processing. Airplane trails, satellite streaks, cosmic ray hits,

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:48.600
and bad pixels appear in the raw version. Software packages including Astro pixel processor,

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:55.060
Deep Sky Stacker and Pix Insight reduced these imperfections without altering the galaxy itself.

00:01:55.660 --> 00:02:00.780
The processed result better matches the true appearance of M31 as seen from Earth.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:05.920
The before image came from a garden observatory during long exposure sessions.

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:13.180
On a different note, Spaceberg gathers professional and amateur participants interested in outer space exploration.

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:18.000
The gathering takes place in Pittsburgh and features discussions on current missions

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.060
and observations.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:24.520
Local organizers highlight the growing community interest in astronomy and spaceflight.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:29.720
Sessions cover both professional updates and hobbyist techniques for viewing the night sky.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:36.440
Next, a geochemical modeling study from Jaxa and the University of Tokyo examines possible

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:38.580
underground carbonate rocks on Mars.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:43.760
The work addresses the apparent shortage of surface carbonates that should have formed

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:44.840
in a wetter past.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:50.160
Models suggest these rocks could lie deep below the surface, preserving evidence of earlier

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:50.980
liquid water.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:56.660
The study focuses on how carbon dioxide from a thicker early atmosphere might have been

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:57.820
sequestered underground.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:03.600
Reports indicate a Chinese Baidu navigation satellite received fuel while in orbit.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:09.160
it. The operation, if confirmed, would mark an advance in on-orbit servicing capabilities.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:15.280
Such technology could extend satellite lifetimes and support future assembly of larger structures.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:21.360
The claims come from sources familiar with Chinese space activities. Astronomers identified

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:27.480
a planet estimated at 1 million years old, still forming within its disk. The object orbits

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:33.920
the young star Elias 224, and represents the earliest stage of planet growth observed so far.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:39.680
Data from multiple telescopes supported the age and location measurements. The discovery

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:44.320
places the planet in the class of worlds still a creating material from its birth environment.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:50.480
Jets from supermassive black holes reach into the circumgalactic medium that surrounds galaxies.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:56.180
This medium holds gas extending 10 to 20 times farther than the visible stellar disk.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:04:02.600
The jets interact with this reservoir, potentially influencing future star formation across the galaxy.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:07.600
Observations show that jets can heat or stir gas at these large distances.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:13.480
Four crew members reached Florida ahead of an October 1st launch to the International Space Station.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:17.480
They will spend approximately six months aboard the orbiting laboratory.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:21.860
The mission continues regular crew rotation between partner agencies.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:27.380
The crew includes astronauts and a cosmonaut preparing for standard handover procedures.

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:33.420
NASA astronaut Luke Delaney from DeBerry, Florida, ready for his upcoming flight to the station.

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:37.960
His selection marks a second mission for the astronaut with deep local ties.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:42.220
Training and preparation continue at Kennedy Space Center facilities.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:47.680
Delaney's background includes prior flights and specialized roles in vehicle systems.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:55.180
Spacecraft guidance systems now simulate docking maneuvers at orbital speeds near 28,000 kilometers per hour.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:01.480
The approach accounts for the absence of atmospheric drag and the need for precise relative positioning.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:06.240
Tests aim to reduce reliance on ground commands during final approach.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:12.040
The algorithms model the relative motion between two vehicles traveling at matching velocities.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:17.760
sensors captured temperature and material loss data inside a heat shield during reentry

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:20.360
conditions above 3000 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:26.140
The measurements track how outer layers erode in a controlled manner to protect the vehicle.

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:30.340
Results will inform design of future thermal protection systems.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:35.020
The tests recorded ablation rates across different sections of the shield's surface.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:42.440
A Falcon 9 lifted off from Vandenberg carrying the secret USSF 385 payload for the Space Force.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:46.640
The booster completed its 10th flight before landing on a drone ship.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:51.660
The mission adds to suspected infrastructure supporting national security satellites.

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:55.840
Recovery operations followed standard procedures for the first stage.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:06:01.080
The company launched a classified payload for the United States Space Force from the California

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:01.580
site.

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:07.820
Videoed and photo rafts documented the lift-off and booster recovery. Details of the satellite

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:13.560
remain undisclosed. The launch used a Falcon 9 configuration typical for national security

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:18.700
missions. Two astronauts who traveled farther from Earth than any previous crew members have

00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:24.360
taken on fresh agency roles. Their experience includes extended deep space operations.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:30.100
The assignments draw on that background for ongoing programs. The new positions focus

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:32.640
on mission planning and crew training support.

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:40.060
On September 26, 2005, the Cassie knee spacecraft completed its initial close fly-by of Saturn's

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:41.040
Moon Hyperion.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:47.240
The irregularly-shaped body rotates chaotically and displays a sponge-like surface texture.

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:52.020
The encounter provided the first detailed images of this unusual satellite.

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:58.060
Hyperion stands out among Saturn's moons for its low-density and heavily cratered appearance.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:04.900
J.W.S.T. observations of Tariqlo captured changes in ring density through stellar occultation

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:06.560
measurements taken years apart.

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:11.300
The inner ring brightened significantly in blocking starlight while the outer ring

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:15.540
dimmed, suggesting ongoing material exchange between the two structures.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:21.600
These shifts occurred over a five-year baseline and point to dynamic processes even around

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:24.420
a small body 125 kilometers across.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:30.600
The findings open questions about how rings around centaurs form and evolve without a large

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:36.220
parent planet to supply debris. What mechanism drives the apparent transfer of material from

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:41.780
one ring to the other? A typical reentry vehicle traveling at orbital speed carries kinetic

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:47.660
energy equivalent to the explosive yield of several tons of TNT concentrated into its heat shield

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:53.340
surface. Picture a shield the size of a large dinner table absorbing that energy while the craft

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:58.740
drops from space to sea level in roughly 8 minutes. The outer layer reaches temperatures

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:04.800
above 3,000 degrees Fahrenheit and literally boils away molecule by molecule, carrying

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:10.900
heat outward instead of inward. Engineers embed sensors that record exactly how fast each

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:17.120
millimeter disappears so the next design can shave off unnecessary mass. One surprising

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:22.620
measurement showed oblation rates varying by more than 20% across a single panel because

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:28.300
of tiny differences in material density. The open puzzle is whether we can ever predict those

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:33.240
local variations well enough to trust an untested shield on a crude return from Mars.

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:38.420
Next time, keep an eye on follow-up observations from the Turiclo Ring Study,

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:44.380
as additional occultation events are scheduled. That covers today's Space and Science news.

